# ── Leverage — environment configuration ────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` for local development. NEVER commit the real `.env`.
#
# ⚠️  SECURITY: this app has NO backend. Every VITE_* variable is inlined
#     into the client bundle at build time and is therefore PUBLIC — it is
#     NOT a secret. Anyone can read it from the shipped JavaScript.
#
#     Protect the YouTube key with restrictions, not secrecy:
#       • API restriction:         YouTube Data API v3 only
#       • Application restriction: HTTP referrers → your deployment domain
#
# Optional. If omitted, the app prompts the user for a key on first run and
# stores it in that browser's localStorage only.
VITE_YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# Gemini is intentionally NOT configurable via build-time env.
# A shared Gemini key in client code would be unrestricted and abusable,
# and securing it would require a backend this app deliberately does not have.
# Users supply their own key in Settings; it stays in their browser.
